<title>GERMANY: Reuters 9th ex-Frankfurt air cargo market report.</title>
<headline>Reuters 9th ex-Frankfurt air cargo market report.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Below are the current average ex-Frankfurt(FRA) German mark air cargo rates per kg for a 100kg shipment, with a volume to weight ratio of six-to-one. These rates are exclusive of cargo fuel surcharges being applied by airlines.</p>
<p>			 Nov15     Oct 14</p>
<p>			  NORTH AMERICA</p>
<p>    FRA-JFK	  1.70	1.65</p>
<p>    FRA-CHI	  1.65	1.60</p>
<p>    FRA-LAX	  1.95	1.90</p>
<p>    FRA-MIA	  2.00	1.95</p>
<p>    FRA-ATL	  1.85	1.80</p>
<p>			 ASIA-PACIFIC</p>
<p>    FRA-SIN	  2.70	2.65</p>
<p>    FRA-BKK	  2.65	2.60</p>
<p>    FRA-KUL	  2.70	2.65</p>
<p>    FRA-HKG	  2.75	2.70</p>
<p>    FRA-SHA	  3.10	3.10</p>
<p>    FRA-SEL	  3.75	3.70</p>
<p>    FRA-NRT	  4.30	4.25</p>
<p>			 LATIN AMERICA</p>
<p>    FRA-SAO	  5.10	5.10</p>
<p>    FRA-EZE (B.A.) 5.30	5.30</p>
<p>    FRA-SCL	  5.30	5.30</p>
<p>			 AFRICA</p>
<p>    FRA-JHB	  4.10	4.10</p>
<p>			 MIDDLE EAST</p>
<p>    FRA-DXB	  1.45	1.40</p>
<p>* The rates quoted in this report were obtained by Reuter journalists on a confidential basis from a range of airlines, large forwarders and smaller air cargo agents based at or near Frankfurt Airport.</p>
<p>* All prices are quoted in German marks.</p>
<p>* The tariffs represent average rates calculated from a range of prices, including standard, discount and spot rates, and are indicative of current market activity. -- Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+44 171 542 5017</p>
</text>
